## Observation
Invalid key yields: assistant message finish:"error", empty content, typed
error {type:"provider.auth",message,status:401,response:{body}}, then idle
outcome:"failed". Quota/rate-limit share the envelope with types
provider.quota / provider.rate-limit (source-mapped), but NO reset-time
field exists anywhere in the schema — a reset instant, if present at all,
is buried in response.body text. So the Dispatcher cannot rely on a reset
timestamp: adopt the fallback — treat any repeated provider refusal as a
usage limit and probe on a timer.

## Verdict: yes (shape observed; quota/reset mapped from source) /
